{
  "schemaVersion": 16,
  "description": "Route reservation under traffic control. Row 1 is plain track from dead end (0,1) to dead end (7,1); A(1,0) has platform (1,1) and B(6,0) platform (6,1). A train holds what it stands on, the node ahead of it (its own node, or the far end of its link) and every link and node of the rest of its continuation. Traffic control cannot be turned on while two trains hold the same track: T1 on the link into (3,1) holds (3,1), where T2 stands. Under it, placing a train, setting a continuation or turning round is refused when another train holds track it needs, naming the lowest such train, and track on a route ahead cannot be removed. T3's service is due to leave A at minute 1, but its whole route to B must be free: it waits while T1 stands at (3,1), then while T2 stands at (4,1), and leaves at minute 4, the first step after both are gone. Standing at B, it holds only its node; its service ends there at minute 12.",
